# Shell scripts keep LF, whatever the platform.
#
# core.autocrlf is on in Git for Windows, so a checkout here gives every text
# file CRLF - and these scripts are not run by Windows. They are run by WSL
# bash during the build and by the device's shell after it, and both take a
# trailing CR as part of the word: `set -euo pipefail\r` comes back as
# "pipefail: invalid option name", and a `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang looks
# for an interpreter that does not exist. The build script that calls them
# then stops with an error about an option name, ten lines from anything to
# do with line endings.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf

# Screens are compared by eye, not by diff.
*.png   binary
*.bmp   binary
